From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 23:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: match SM8150 streaming DMA contract

Test20 reached START_DONE, queued four FTBs, and reset after the first
encoder ETB. The 64-byte ETB packet and its populated fields match the
Xiaomi VPU5 packet. The IOVAs, sizes, route, mode, core, internal buffers,
clocks, and bandwidth vote also pass the recorded contracts.

The remaining memory contract did not match. Xiaomi maps video dma-bufs as
streaming DMA with the upstream-cache hint. It performs explicit cache
maintenance at QBUF and DQBUF. Patch 0033 applied the cacheable IOMMU hint
to VB2 coherent MMAP allocations. That combination no longer has coherent
DMA semantics and performs no VB2 prepare or finish synchronization.

Force IRIS1 encoder MMAP queues through VB2's non-coherent allocation path.
It allocates a contiguous IOVA with the upstream hint and performs the
required DMA synchronization around ownership transfers. Reject an encoder
MMAP buffer if that contract is not active, and log the allocation mode.
Imported DMABUF behavior is unchanged.

Also order the ETB assignments like its wire structure and Xiaomi's
packetizer. The packet bytes do not change, but the exact layout becomes
mechanically auditable. Rename count diagnostics to reflect that INPUT 16/3
and OUTPUT 4/2 are vendor-style requests. The post-count firmware table may
report OUTPUT min 4 without another wire count command.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@openai.com>
---
diff --git a/Documentation/core-api/dma-attributes.rst b/Documentation/core-api/dma-attributes.rst
index a664d03bdb03..d8fac18b3f81 100644
--- a/Documentation/core-api/dma-attributes.rst
+++ b/Documentation/core-api/dma-attributes.rst
@@ -186,4 +186,6 @@ DMA_ATTR_IOMMU_USE_UPSTREAM_HINT
 This attribute requests the IOMMU page-table memory type that forwards cache
 allocation policy to the upstream interconnect. It is intended for integrated
 devices whose system-cache contract requires the upstream transaction hint.
-Architectures without such a memory type may ignore the attribute.
+Architectures without such a memory type may ignore the attribute. The
+attribute does not make a mapping coherent; streaming mappings must still use
+the DMA API synchronization required by their direction and ownership.
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_cmds.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_cmds.c
index 4741d2d3471d..fadd1922766b 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_cmds.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_cmds.c
@@ -323,9 +323,9 @@ int pkt_session_etb_encoder(
 	pkt->flags = in_frame->flags;
 	pkt->mark_target = in_frame->mark_target;
 	pkt->mark_data = in_frame->mark_data;
-	pkt->offset = in_frame->offset;
 	pkt->alloc_len = in_frame->alloc_len;
 	pkt->filled_len = in_frame->filled_len;
+	pkt->offset = in_frame->offset;
 	pkt->input_tag = in_frame->clnt_data;
 	pkt->packet_buffer = in_frame->device_addr;
 	pkt->extradata_buffer = in_frame->extradata_addr;
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
index 7954af607b8d..4fd92e6ef5e0 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
@@ -1486,7 +1486,7 @@ static int venc_iris1_set_buffer_count(struct venus_inst *inst, u32 type,
 		return ret;
 
 	dev_info(inst->core->dev,
-		 "venus-sm8150: encoder final count type=%#x actual=%u host-min=%u committed\n",
+		 "venus-sm8150: encoder count request type=%#x actual=%u host-min=%u committed\n",
 		 type, count, actual.count_min_host);
 
 	return 0;
@@ -1503,6 +1503,16 @@ static int venc_queue_setup(struct vb2_queue *q,
 	enum hfi_version ver = core->res->hfi_version;
 	int ret, pm_ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * Downstream maps encoder dma-bufs as streaming, bidirectional memory,
+	 * applies the upstream cache hint, and performs cache maintenance at
+	 * QBUF/DQBUF.  Coherent MMAP allocations cannot safely use that cacheable
+	 * IOMMU attribute, so make VB2 use its non-coherent allocation path.  VB2
+	 * then performs the matching sync in its prepare/finish callbacks.
+	 */
+	if (IS_IRIS1(core) && q->memory == VB2_MEMORY_MMAP)
+		q->non_coherent_mem = 1;
+
 	if (*num_planes) {
 		if (q->type == V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_OUTPUT_MPLANE &&
 		    *num_planes != inst->fmt_out->num_planes)
@@ -1625,6 +1635,15 @@ static int venc_buf_init(struct vb2_buffer *vb)
 	struct venus_buffer *buf = to_venus_buffer(vbuf);
 	int ret;
 
+	if (IS_IRIS1(inst->core) && vb->vb2_queue->memory == VB2_MEMORY_MMAP &&
+	    (!vb->vb2_queue->non_coherent_mem ||
+	     !(vb->vb2_queue->dma_attrs &
+	       DMA_ATTR_IOMMU_USE_UPSTREAM_HINT))) {
+		dev_err(inst->core->dev,
+			"unsafe IRIS1 encoder MMAP cache contract\n");
+		return -EINVAL;
+	}
+
 	inst->buf_count++;
 
 	ret = venus_helper_vb2_buf_init(vb);
@@ -1632,12 +1651,15 @@ static int venc_buf_init(struct vb2_buffer *vb)
 		inst->buf_count--;
 		return ret;
 	}
-
-	if (IS_IRIS1(inst->core) && V4L2_TYPE_IS_OUTPUT(vb->type))
+	if (IS_IRIS1(inst->core))
 		dev_info(inst->core->dev,
-			 "venus-sm8150: encoder input buffer index=%u length=%lu dma=%pad bidirectional=%u\n",
+			 "venus-sm8150: enc %s buf=%u len=%lu dma=%pad bidi=%u nc=%u up=%u\n",
+			 V4L2_TYPE_IS_OUTPUT(vb->type) ? "input" : "bitstream",
 			 vb->index, vb2_plane_size(vb, 0), &buf->dma_addr,
-			 vb->vb2_queue->bidirectional);
+			 vb->vb2_queue->bidirectional,
+			 vb->vb2_queue->non_coherent_mem,
+			 !!(vb->vb2_queue->dma_attrs &
+			    DMA_ATTR_IOMMU_USE_UPSTREAM_HINT));
 
 	return 0;
 }
@@ -1955,10 +1977,12 @@ static int venc_start_streaming(struct vb2_queue *q, unsigned int count)
 
 	if (IS_IRIS1(inst->core)) {
 		/*
-		 * Both final counts are now reflected in the refreshed table.
+		 * Cache the firmware table after the vendor-style count requests.
+		 * External counts stay owned by VB2; this refreshed copy supplies
+		 * internal sizes/counts and validates the negotiated allocations.
 		 */
 		dev_info(inst->core->dev,
-			 "venus-sm8150: final encoder buffer requirements cached\n");
+			 "venus-sm8150: post-count encoder requirements cached\n");
 
 		/*
 		 * Downstream names wire property 0x20100c BUFFER_SIZE_MINIMUM and
